#: NAVIGATION.md:1
msgid "Tutorial - Advanced mechanical pulling"
msgstr ""

#: NAVIGATION.md:3
msgid ""
"This goes beyond what was presented in PLUMED Masterclass 22.15, and which "
"is now available as a Tutorial on [this page](https://www.plumed-"
"tutorials.org/lessons/22/015/data/NAVIGATION.html)"
msgstr ""

#: NAVIGATION.md:5
msgid ""
"This tutorial provides theoretical background then gives a set of exercises "
"for you to complete. You may want to watch the videos that accompany the "
"previous tutorial first."
msgstr ""

#: NAVIGATION.md:7
msgid ""
"The flow chart shown below indicates the order in which you should consult "
"the resources. You can click on the nodes to access the various resources. "
"Follow the thick black lines for the best results. The resources that are "
"connected by dashed lines are supplmentary resources that you may find "
"useful when completing the exercise."
msgstr ""
"下のフローチャートは資料を参照する順序を示している。各ノードをクリックすると資料を開ける。太い黒線に沿って進めることを推奨する。破線でつながる資料は、演習に取り組む際に役立つ補足資料である。"

#: NAVIGATION.md:9
msgid ""
"Some relevant perspective articles to consider are [this "
"one](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jpcb.1c06330) from Hocky and [this "
"one](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jpcb.1c10715) from Stirnemann."
msgstr ""

#: NAVIGATION.md:11
msgid ""
"Solutions are available from [This page](https://github.com/hockyg/plumed-"
"tutorial-force2)"
msgstr ""

